dialect protocol
protocol stdio.dxf.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.dxf
start record

# P2-FG1: REAL binary op frame, replacing F6's `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut
# (`../🦀️.rs`'s upgraded `OpBinary` impl, `#region OpCodecs`). `DxfMutation` is a
# genuine data-carrying enum whose variants embed recursive/data-carrying payloads (`DxfSnapshot`,
# `DxfEntity`, `DxfBlock` — itself containing `Vec<DxfEntity>`) — no `DslField` impl exists or can
# exist for any of them (confirmed by a real `cargo check` rejection of
# `#[derive(dsl::DslOps)]`, see that file's own module doc comment), so the generic
# `format u8 | ordinal varint | record body` layout genuinely does not fit. Handcrafted instead:
# `format u8` (`store::pack_rt::OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `tag u8` (the `DxfMutation`
# variant ordinal, same 0-17 order `parse_dxf_mutation`'s own keyword match uses) as two REAL
# fixed fields, then the variant's own recursive payload as one opaque trailing `bytes` chain.
#
# The recursive payload itself is real varint/length-prefixed binary
# (`enc_dxf_snapshot_bin`/`enc_dxf_entity_bin`/`enc_block_bin`/… in `../../🔺️diff/🦀️.rs`'s
# `#region 🔖️ItemBinaryCodecs`, reusing `store::pack_rt::write_varint_u64`/`store::ByteReader`) —
# NOT re-modeled field-by-field here because `Prim::Ref` (the only construct that could describe
# this self-recursion at the protocol-dialect level) unconditionally errors during `walk_protocol`
# (confirmed live, `protocol-prim-ref-recursion` in the recipe's own consolidated gap table — every
# P1-P3 pilot independently hit and worked around the same wall). This is the same honest-boundary
# treatment the plan prescribes for a compressed/recursive payload segment — opaque at the
# protocol layer, genuinely structured (and round-trip-tested) at the Rust layer.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8
chain payload bytes
